 "returned_to_tern": {
  "capacity_restriction_affecting_ack_and_detection": "timeout-ack and the liveness check are in the 'due' class (cap 3) with the deadline callbacks. When 3 due writers are queued, a timeout-ack or a check is refused AT ONCE with E_LEDGER_SATURATED, and must be retried (the check's next timer run in 30 s; a person's ack by hand). Deadline detection is not lost, because a refused callback writes its due marker, but ack latency under a deadline burst depends on this cap. Options for your ruling: a separate 'ack' class, or exempting timeout-ack and check from the due cap. Not changed without a grant."
 },
